<p></p>
<h1 data-nh-numbering=3D"1." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Overview"><u><stro=
ng>Overview</strong></u></h1>
<p>This document reviews whether the current BaRS design can support patien=
t-facing appointment access through the NHS App, with particular focus on a=
uthentication, routing, API behaviour, scale and security.</p>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"1.1." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-HowtheNHSAppcoul=
daccessappointments">How the NHS App could access appointments</h2>
<p>The NHS App would authenticate the user through the NHS Identity flow al=
ready used in the GP Connect PF changes, then call the BaRS API over HTTPS.=
 Apigee would validate the token and required scope before the BaRS proxy r=
outes the request. For standard appointment requests, BaRS would use the ca=
ller-supplied <code>NHSD-Target-Identifier</code> to read the provider endp=
oint from the S3 routing registry, then forward the FHIR request to the NME=
 provider over mTLS. BaRS does not currently handle NHS Identity tokens or =
patient-level delegated authorisation, so changes around token handling and=
 patient-matching check must be implemented before this flow is supported.<=
/p>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"1.2." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Changesrequired"=
>Changes required</h2>
<p>The main changes are expected in APIM and the BaRS proxy. Accepting and =
decoding the NHS Identity token, preserving the required delegation context=
, and checking the authorized identity against the requested patient before=
 routing. The OpenAPI specification and BaRS Standard will need to document=
 the new token, identity, patient-identifier, and error rules. Providers wi=
ll need to meet the agreed FHIR, mTLS, and authorisation contract. The exis=
ting downstream routing model should remain unchanged unless the agreed PF =
design requires otherwise.</p>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"1.3." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Scale">Scale</h2=
>
<p>The proxy is stateless and can likely scale horizontally. However, every=
 standard request is currently S3 dependent for the routing lookup and a pr=
ovider response. Appointment searches are unpaginated, and retrieval across=
 multiple providers may require multiple calls. The planned <code>_include<=
/code> uplift may increase response size and provider load. Load, response-=
size and latency would be something I would want to look at post <code>_inc=
lude</code> addition to ensure timings are still within agreed performance =
bands.</p>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"1.4." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Identityanddatap=
rotection">Identity and data protection</h2>
<p>The current design protects transport with HTTPS and provider mTLS, stor=
es secrets in Apigee KVMs, uses AWS Signature for S3, and uses a separate c=
ached token for NRLF. The current BaRS flow does not handle NHS Identity to=
kens or forward demonstrated end-user claims to providers. Logging, tracing=
, token forwarding, NHS-number handling, and FHIR payload redaction depend =
partly on external Apigee and Splunk configuration and require confirmation=
.</p>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"1.5." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Routing(Current&=
amp;Future)">Routing (Current &amp; Future)</h2>
<p>Today, standard provider endpoints are resolved from the S3 routing file=
 using <code>NHSD-Target-Identifier</code> and a path-to-endpoint mapping. =
<code>DocumentReference</code> uses fixed NRLF routes. Another team is plan=
ning to move EPC from a flat file to its own service. That may change the i=
nterface and ownership, but it is not a change being made by DI so would be=
 a case of working with the team rather than owning that work ourselves.</p=
>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"1.6." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Reuseandstandard=
isation">Reuse and standardisation</h2>
<p>The standard provider route is largely provider-neutral. Existing provid=
er URLs are configuration-driven and requests use the agreed FHIR and mTLS =
interfaces. Reuse beyond Medicus is possible where providers support the sa=
me endpoint keys, FHIR contracts, certificates, and operational requirement=
s.</p>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"1.7." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Remainingrisksan=
ddecisions">Remaining risks and decisions</h2>
<p>The main risk items are the PF authorisation changes and claims, <code>_=
include</code> semantics and response limits, provider conformance, S3 and =
future EPC availability, rate limits, timeout and retry behaviour, logging =
redaction, and cross-team ownership of releases and operational processes (=
DI, BaRS, EPC Changes, Documentation, Releases etc).</p>
<p><br></p>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manu=
