<p><code class=3D"language-mermaid"> </code></p>
<pre><br></pre>
<hr>
<h1 data-nh-numbering=3D"2." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Authentication&amp=
;TokenExchange"><u><strong>A</strong><strong>uthentication &amp; Token Exch=
ange</strong></u></h1>
<p>This section explains how callers and downstream services authenticate, =
and how the planned PF authentication model may change that flow.</p>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"2.1." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-CurrentImplement=
ation">Current Implementation</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"9f8946b8-2bd3-4181-af00-f9bbe29ebffb">BaRS authenticates =
callers in Apigee with a Bearer OAuth access token and the booking-and-refe=
rral scope.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"18fc914f-bb04-4cf3-89ee-516e0b4eb669">The live proxy chec=
ks the token before it routes the request, reads S3, or calls another servi=
ce.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"55269448-ec1a-464a-947a-f6c3f5cea545">BaRS calls provider=
 systems using its own client certificate and mTLS.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"c1d01f88-3ecf-45ad-bf63-bc40d2153e92"><code>DocumentRefer=
ence</code> requests use a separate NRLF flow. BaRS creates a client assert=
ion JWT, gets an NRLF access token, caches it, and uses it for the NRLF req=
uest.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"0e60d664-0eea-42f1-a2b4-fcb611a58837">BaRS does not accep=
t, validate, decode, or exchange NHS Identity tokens. It also does not comp=
are delegated-access claims with patient identifiers in FHIR requests.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"180c674c-f51e-4b5a-bc81-7dbf1b98f7c1">In the GP Connect P=
F approach, the aggregator verifies NHS Identity and uses private-JWT OAuth=
 flows. Its current verification returns only the date of birth. It does no=
t keep the <code>act</code>, subject, actor, or NHS-number claims needed fo=
r a BaRS authorisation decision.</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"2.2." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Post-PFBehaviour=
">Post-PF Behaviour</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"7fe39ea3-4cf6-4cce-9f54-7b8af3fc5d91">A PF consumer or mi=
d flow service will authenticate the user with NHS Identity and obtain the =
agreed PF access token.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"58c93b54-c5b7-4763-98a1-e942eb1b8284">BaRS will need to v=
alidate that token and any delegated subject, actor, or <code>act</code> in=
formation it contains.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"63c4827a-0082-4ef8-92e9-db5e84cf121e">BaRS should check t=
hat the user is allowed to access the requested patient before it routes or=
 forwards the request.</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"2.3." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-PFChangesNeeded"=
>PF Changes Needed</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"12fe06c7-f825-4b87-ba7d-baad571fa03e"><strong>APIM and Ba=
RS Proxy:</strong> Add the PF token checks after OAuth validation and befor=
e any S3, NRLF, or provider call.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"f596521c-ab1f-40f4-a390-ad3134218616"><strong>Token excha=
nge:</strong> Confirm that the exchanged token keeps the delegation informa=
tion BaRS needs. The aggregator's client assertion <code>sub</code> identif=
ies the aggregator, not the end user.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"a63220a3-ef23-4e98-a7e1-7ca09553fe4c"><strong>OpenAPI and=
 BaRS Standard:</strong> Document the token, delegation, patient-identifier=
, scope, and error-response rules.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"91973f36-90f9-481c-89e9-ad25f3ec3aab"><strong>Providers:<=
/strong> Decide whether BaRS alone checks patient access or whether every p=
rovider must also understand the user's identity.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"b7197960-5e58-445e-a9ae-230b98343c3b"><strong>Testing:</s=
trong> Test matching and mismatching patients, missing claims, expired toke=
ns, rejected requests, and downstream authentication failures.</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"2.4." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-CurrentRisks">Cu=
rrent Risks</h2>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"confluenceTable">
  <thead class=3D"">
   <tr class=3D"">
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Risk</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Potential impact</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Information</th>
   </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody class=3D"">
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Provider authentication is unavailable</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Requests fail even when the caller's token i=
s valid.</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">The live service has a 32-second timeout. Re=
try behaviour is not defined in this repository.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">NRLF token cache is not sufficiently isolate=
d</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">A token could be reused for the wrong client=
 or authorisation context.</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">The cache key is always <code>nrlfAccessToke=
n</code>. Confirm that this is safe, or include the client or audience in t=
he key.</td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"2.5." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-FutureRequiremen=
ts">Future Requirements</h2>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"confluenceTable">
  <thead class=3D"">
   <tr class=3D"">
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">PF requirement</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">What must be resolved</th>
   </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody class=3D"">
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Patient authorisation</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Check the user's authority against the patie=
nt identifier before any downstream call.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Provider identity behaviour</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Decide whether BaRS checks access alone or w=
hether providers also need user information.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Token forwarding</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Define which credential is used at each boun=
dary to ensure minimal sharing of NHS tokens.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Cross-component ownership</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Coordinate changes across APIM, BaRS Proxy, =
token exchange, OAS, the BaRS Standard, providers, testing, and operations.=
</td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"2.6." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Considerations">=
Considerations</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"e6c72578-2dd5-4a3a-9e9c-021b5221ae61">Token lifetimes dif=
fer by flow.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"86b87d2c-3333-4412-93c0-dc157e2eb610">No retry policy is =
shown for token endpoints or provider authentication.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"817b5413-6188-4c9d-a084-fab63d90dc43">Authentication fail=
ures should use BaRS's existing FHIR <code>OperationOutcome</code> format.<=
/li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"09256385-c567-420c-9500-3e033c0ac685">Existing proxy requ=
irements include the BaRS scope, API product and client registration, mTLS,=
 KVM values, and shared flows.</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"2.7." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-OpenQuestions">O=
pen Questions</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"567753fd-4eb8-496a-9070-1e0ae79bd9a5">Does the exchanged =
token preserve the delegation information BaRS needs? When it reaches BaRS,=
 is it a JWT, an opaque token, or an introspectable token?</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"d4458c50-1c90-4121-b9f7-a5e7171c6168">Which claims identi=
fy the subject, actor, and delegation?</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"e7c4730d-731c-4c94-af4a-dda926bf3d31">Which endpoints nee=
d patient matching, and how should the NHS number be extracted from searche=
s and <code>$process-message</code> bundles?</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"1f3bb517-79f9-4613-9e6c-9ff40484ef28">What response shoul=
d BaRS return when delegation is missing, invalid, expired, or does not mat=
ch the requested patient?</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"c0113e78-d7fb-4fb9-92c6-fe8ebe960eea">Who owns the long-t=
erm authentication contract across APIM, BaRS, the BaRS Standard, and provi=
der systems?</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"2.8." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-ExistingProcessF=
low">Existing Process Flow</h2>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manu=
al-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" width=
