<h1 data-nh-numbering=3D"3." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Scalability"><u><s=
trong>Scalability</strong></u></h1>
<p>This section explains how the current architecture handles traffic, prov=
ider demand &amp; response sizes.</p>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"3.1." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-CurrentImplement=
ation.1">Current Implementation</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"85e16845-cc45-412f-85be-294225bbb829">The live proxy is s=
tateless. Each request is routed independently, so the proxy layer can scal=
e.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"85cccf31-69a6-4dc0-9c44-4d837d24cab9">Standard provider r=
equests fetch the routing configuration from S3 on every request before res=
olving the provider endpoint.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"3350935f-ac12-4cd6-be03-7e627849c968">The S3 request requ=
ires KVM credential reads, AWS Signature Version 4 signing, and an external=
 service callout.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"0a19e9a9-d129-4924-a787-7c09bd64135c">NRLF access tokens =
are cached for 300 seconds, reducing repeated token exchanges.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"191eb0ce-9a84-4028-af26-d4df7b76291f">Rate limiting is pr=
ovided by an external Apigee shared flow.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"c66631c3-8de1-483c-ae0c-eae347d4c1e9">Provider connection=
s and connection reuse are managed by Apigee; the specifics are not defined=
 in this repository.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"04c16cc6-9e9d-4518-9d79-6fc28b0cd15f">The standard provid=
er target has a 32-second timeout. No equivalent explicit timeout is define=
d for the S3 or NRLF service callouts in the repository.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"3daef494-3b4e-44f1-99b7-40301c10d01f">No request retry or=
 circuit-breaker policy is defined in the repository.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"e6fe005e-8ed4-4f2c-aa7c-00fa593d907e">Appointment searche=
s return all matching appointments for a patient at a provider. No paginati=
on, date filter, or status filter is currently defined.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"50c08f23-e21b-4a64-a693-4821a994bcae">A caller that needs=
 results from multiple providers must make one request per provider and com=
bine the responses itself.</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"3.2." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-CurrentFlow">Cur=
rent Flow</h2>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manu=
al-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" width=
=3D"468" src=3D"c54ac496961942ca5a8a8609b8f4d89d8364c046509677df24c7179cb09=
cd831" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachments/1485019956/mermaid-flowchart=
-2026-08-27T19-48-29.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1787920386938&a=
mp;api=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D=
"1485019959" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=
=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"mermaid-flowchart-202=
6-08-27T19-48-29.png" data-base-url=3D"https://nhsd-confluence.digital.nhs.=
uk" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-co=
ntainer-id=3D"1485019956" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"1" tabi=
ndex=3D"0" alt=3D"" height=3D"779"></span></p>
<pre><br></pre>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"3.3." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Post-PFBehaviour=
.1">Post-PF Behaviour</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"94568939-01b3-40c4-a2ba-35779add546e">The PF service shou=
ld support the expected patient retrieval volume without assuming that one =
provider or one small response represents the whole workload.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"f43d1ec2-11c7-4121-a323-efec5130439f">The planned FHIR <c=
ode>_include</code> uplift should allow a search response to include linked=
 resources, but it must not be treated as a replacement for pagination or o=
ther result-size controls.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"b2adfd19-2056-47d0-88af-8d74c8f97123">Routing configurati=
on should be available with controlled latency and defined behaviour when S=
3 is slow or unavailable.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"ba3a05ad-ca9f-4ae0-b9c4-c37726cb1782">Provider fan-out, r=
esponse aggregation, rate limits, timeouts, and failure handling should be =
measured under realistic PF workloads.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"4734ca47-8ed1-4eca-9e7c-fd3044ea96fa">Any new caching mus=
t define freshness, stale-data, invalidation, cache scope, and recovery beh=
aviour.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"ee3924f1-c7ea-44b6-8613-f62ddd61d07a">Retry behaviour mus=
t be explicit and safe for the operation. Blind retries must not duplicate =
booking or other non-idempotent requests.</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"3.4." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-ChangesNeeded">C=
hanges Needed</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"d96665fa-d16c-4937-9c23-9ab20efb4c80"><strong>Routing cac=
he:</strong> Assess an Apigee cache for the S3 routing document, with versi=
oning and refresh rules.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"51e3c9be-ab89-45cc-909c-be1168ab46a3"><strong>API / OpenA=
PI:</strong> Define useful filters if the expected appointment result set c=
an be large. Document <code>_include</code>, supported reference paths, res=
ponse semantics, and invalid-value handling.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"b2825119-a207-474b-8bee-04700b06cad5"><strong>BaRS Standa=
rd:</strong> Define provider expectations for filters, <code>_include</code=
>, response limits, timeouts, and errors.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"4cde9408-a5f9-43e0-847e-3cc24278eafd"><strong>Provider ca=
pacity:</strong> Test provider connection limits, response latency, concurr=
ent requests, and behaviour when a provider is slow or unavailable.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"0d179edf-75fc-46a2-8b01-f63b6f9b1a97"><strong>Resilience:=
</strong> Define timeouts, retry rules, idempotency handling, circuit break=
ing, and partial-failure behaviour.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"00522ca8-2b85-4109-99db-49b1c8e07be7"><strong>Testing:</s=
trong> Add dependency-failure, large-response, and <code>_include</code> te=
sts.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"a88a2e87-92cb-4932-9835-fc41d6b0c4ab"><strong>Observabili=
ty:</strong> Measure S3 latency, provider latency, response size, cache hit=
 rate, throttling, failures, and downstream concurrency.</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"3.5." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-CurrentRisks.1">=
Current Risks</h2>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"confluenceTable">
  <thead class=3D"">
   <tr class=3D"">
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Risk</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Potential impact</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Evidence or mitigation</th>
   </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody class=3D"">
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">S3 lookup on every standard request</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">S3 latency or failure affects every routed r=
equest and limits throughput.</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">No routing-document cache was found. Measure=
 the dependency and define cache or fallback behaviour.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Appointment result sets are unbounded</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Large responses can increase latency, memory=
 use, transfer time, and client processing.</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">No pagination, date filter, or status filter=
 is defined.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Rate-limit behaviour is not visible in this =
repository</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">The configured limit may not match the inten=
ded production workload or may not isolate clients fairly.</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Inspect the external shared flow and deploye=
d quotas.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Timeout and retry behaviour is incomplete</t=
d>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Slow dependencies may hold connections open,=
 while unsafe retries could duplicate non-idempotent operations.</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Provider timeout is 32 seconds; S3/NRLF time=
out and request retry rules need confirmation.</td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"3.6." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-FutureRequiremen=
ts.1">Future Requirements</h2>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"confluenceTable">
  <thead class=3D"">
   <tr class=3D"">
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Requirement</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">What must be resolved</th>
   </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody class=3D"">
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><code>_include</code> support</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Define allowed reference paths, response str=
ucture, provider support, and handling of invalid or unsupported values.</t=
d>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Response-size control</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Decide whether pagination, date/status filte=
rs, maximum bundle size, or other limits are needed alongside <code>_includ=
e</code>.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Multi-provider retrieval</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Define whether PF performs sequential or par=
allel calls, how it limits fan-out, and how it handles partial results.</td=
>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Routing availability</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Define how current routing data is refreshed=
, cached, versioned, and recovered after S3 failure.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Safe retries</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Identify idempotent operations and define ho=
w booking operations avoid duplicate requests.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Provider conformance</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Confirm the minimum provider behaviour for f=
ilters, <code>_include</code>, timeouts, response limits, and errors.</td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"3.7." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Considerations.1=
">Considerations</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"ef0fdab9-4cba-4fdf-8133-2e7e606ac2c0"><code>_include</cod=
e> may increase the number of resources in a <code>Bundle</code> even when =
the number of matching appointments is unchanged.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"1af5d425-4018-4674-9109-d4216464ce91">An unbounded appoin=
tment search combined with <code>_include</code> could produce a significan=
tly larger response than the current response model.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"e7e88765-2ec1-4a1c-bdab-0cb359eedb1e">A PF client retriev=
ing several providers may create a fan-out pattern that multiplies provider=
 load and increases end-to-end latency.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"041be05c-5b18-4230-9fde-f09d98181d45">Retry decisions mus=
t distinguish safe reads from non-idempotent booking operations.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"d3c726e1-2675-4b70-a5c6-b2ccfcdaff39">Caching, rate limit=
s, and capacity will likely be affected by <code>_include</code> and should=
 be reviewed when the uplift is defined.</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"3.8." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-OpenQuestions.1"=
>Open Questions</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"6ee2cf28-013a-4113-baae-210849ae00dd">What throughput, la=
tency, concurrency, and response-size targets must be supported?</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"334294cf-8646-4297-b533-02d591b84540">Should appointment =
searches gain pagination, date filtering, status filtering, or a maximum re=
sponse size alongside <code>_include</code>?</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"68180bf6-9875-4103-8bdd-07b6ee41a2be">Are the existing ra=
te limits and timeouts still appropriate with <code>_include</code>?</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"49e5ff15-d5a6-47d7-9a25-79f212037271">With the inclusion =
of <code>_include</code>, how should scalability be measured, and do the pr=
evious targets or thresholds need to change?</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h1 data-nh-numbering=3D"4." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Security"><strong>=
<u>Security</u></strong></h1>
<p>This section summarises the security controls, trust boundaries, and dat=
a-protection considerations within BaRS.</p>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"4.1." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-CurrentImplement=
ation.2">Current Implementation</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"33ff390e-2db8-49cd-a140-6adb819cbf7f">Apigee validates OA=
uth access tokens and the BaRS scope for the live API's protected routes.</=
li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"d2b69276-5485-406a-b2f7-6fd6e5afcfbf">BaRS connects to st=
andard provider systems using its client certificate and mTLS.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"9a19f4d6-32be-4dc9-9537-da1d1e4fe156">BaRS uses AWS Signa=
ture to access the private S3 routing registry.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"88b5b7ec-bf4e-461d-94fd-da233e018373">S3 credentials, NRL=
F configuration, and NRLF private keys are stored in Apigee KVMs rather tha=
n in the proxy source.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"56a0ec20-4556-43da-b36c-01129665e52c">NRLF access tokens =
are cached in Apigee for five minutes.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"1a26e085-1513-44fe-bbb9-36a7036a4fa8">Rate limiting and a=
udit logging are provided through Apigee shared flows.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"4b6bba8a-6695-401d-b5dc-955dc2bc5675">The live proxy norm=
alises many failures into FHIR <code>OperationOutcome</code> responses.</li=
>
 <li data-uuid=3D"4c6df5f5-1d14-4dff-8c00-7f18878c5ba5">The repository does=
 not contain the actual secret values, but several important controls depen=
d on external Apigee, AWS, shared-flow, certificate, and logging configurat=
ion.</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"4.2." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-CurrentSecurityB=
oundary">Current Security Boundary</h2>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manu=
al-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" width=
=3D"468" src=3D"e2a2724f5f84919a7a128300c0c3f96e305942232d9d4b3401984141187=
0cc78" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachments/1485019956/mermaid-flowchart=
-2026-08-27T19-49-14.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1787920387497&a=
mp;api=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D=
"1485019960" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=
=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"mermaid-flowchart-202=
6-08-27T19-49-14.png" data-base-url=3D"https://nhsd-confluence.digital.nhs.=
uk" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-co=
ntainer-id=3D"1485019956" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"1" tabi=
ndex=3D"0" alt=3D"" height=3D"130"></span></p>
<p>Current Trust Model:</p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"f055081f-3b58-4d59-81ba-11376b3f72be">The caller authenti=
cates to BaRS with an OAuth access token.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"44d2be36-bc31-4008-b4b3-e693cd422606">BaRS authenticates =
to provider systems with its own mTLS certificate.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"7c45416c-c659-407b-93f0-983c17b8b9d8">BaRS authenticates =
to NRLF with a separate service token.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"d6378e98-d0d0-444b-9366-cc04aa9443f5">Providers therefore=
 trust BaRS as the authenticated client. They do not receive a demonstrated=
 end-user identity from the current flow.</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"4.3." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-IntendedFutureBe=
haviour">Intended Future Behaviour</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"95511aee-4f7d-4f64-b744-de0c173b97b6">PF requests must us=
e the agreed NHS Identity and delegated-access token model.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"33517bd7-3c55-4346-83d0-4c81d01261bd">Patient authorisati=
on must be checked before BaRS routes or forwards a request.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"8c4235f0-ba77-48e6-b6e6-ad6d1f93bca2">The PF design must =
define which identity information is passed between the consumer, BaRS, and=
 provider systems.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"d75b7de4-f8db-49e5-a977-364527fc24a5"><code>_include</cod=
e> must not allow a caller to retrieve linked resources outside the authori=
sation scope of the original request.</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"4.4." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-ChangesNeeded.1"=
>Changes Needed</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"a54cdfc3-f745-48e4-ae6b-2fcfd77b444a"><strong>APIM and Ba=
RS Proxy:</strong> Add the agreed PF token validation and delegated patient=
-authorisation check before routing or downstream calls.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"e671adf5-8b01-4011-af71-bcf90337eefb"><strong>API / OpenA=
PI:</strong> Document security schemes, scopes, required headers, patient-i=
dentifier rules, <code>_include</code> behaviour, and error responses.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"ce837432-0485-4036-adf0-d72210fee1ec"><strong>Provider ca=
pabilities:</strong> Confirm mTLS, certificate rotation, supported identity=
 context, and consistent authorisation behaviour.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"1629256e-081d-4ef6-8574-fbc99da64fb2"><strong>Logging:</s=
trong> Confirm that tokens, client assertions, NHS numbers, target identifi=
ers, and FHIR payloads are excluded or redacted.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"c9b24163-58e0-4b87-bef4-8865f475bf7f"><strong>Testing:</s=
trong> Test invalid and expired tokens, authorisation mismatches, <code>_in=
clude</code> access boundaries, no-downstream-call failures, certificate fa=
ilures, and dependency failures.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"3f0b588d-81ca-4cc1-85f1-b1aed8e971b7"><strong>Documentati=
on:</strong> Document both technical changes and process changes, including=
 incident and recovery procedures.</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"4.5." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-CurrentRisks.2">=
Current Risks</h2>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"confluenceTable">
  <thead class=3D"">
   <tr class=3D"">
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Risk</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Potential impact</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Evidence or mitigation</th>
   </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody class=3D"">
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Sensitive values may be logged</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">OAuth tokens, client assertions, target iden=
tifiers, NHS numbers, or FHIR data could be exposed in logs or traces.</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">The Splunk shared flow is external. <code>JC=
-AWSSignV4.xml</code> also has <code>debug=3Dtrue</code>. Confirm the loggi=
ng behaviour and redaction settings.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">NRLF token cache isolation is unconfirmed</t=
d>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">A cached token could be reused for the wrong=
 client or authorisation context.</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">The cache key is constant: <code>nrlfAccessT=
oken</code>. Confirm its intended scope or isolate the key.</td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"4.6." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Future-StateRequ=
irements">Future-State Requirements</h2>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"confluenceTable">
  <thead class=3D"">
   <tr class=3D"">
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Requirement</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">What must be resolved</th>
   </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody class=3D"">
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Patient-level authorisation</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Define how the authorized identity is matche=
d to the patient in each supported request.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Linked-resource authorisation</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Define whether <code>_include</code> is limi=
ted to references from authorized resources and how provider responses are =
checked.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Token handling</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Define the credential used at each trust bou=
ndary and prohibit unnecessary token forwarding.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Provider consistency</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Define the minimum security, identity, mTLS,=
 and authorisation behaviour required from every provider.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Data protection</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Confirm log redaction, retention, encryption=
, access control, and incident response for NHS numbers and FHIR data. Thes=
e controls are external to this repository, although they should already ex=
ist in the live service.</td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"4.7." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Considerations.2=
">Considerations</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"334f3bf9-a786-48bb-a21d-80787dddea13"><code>_include</cod=
e> may return more sensitive data in one response, so response filtering an=
d authorisation boundaries need to be explicit.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"0cf41f36-6f91-40e5-9ee2-16ee467dbb65">mTLS authenticates =
BaRS to a provider. It does not by itself prove that the end user is author=
ized to access a patient.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"6c1297bb-bea4-441c-b1b8-6c515b42e231">A valid OAuth token=
 proves that a client can call BaRS. Under the current application-level de=
sign, that is the intended authorisation boundary; PF may require an additi=
onal check that binds the user to the requested patient.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"b23c69e9-f10e-453a-8ebe-afae01eed0e6">Any retries, cachin=
g, debugging, or tracing must avoid exposing PII, credentials, or duplicati=
ng sensitive operations.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h1 data-nh-numbering=3D"5." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-EndpointDiscovery/=
EPC"><strong><u>Endpoint Discovery / EPC</u></strong></h1>
<p>This section explains how BaRS resolves provider endpoints today.</p>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"5.1." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-CurrentImplement=
ation.3">Current Implementation</h2>
<p>BaRS currently resolves standard provider endpoints from a flat routing =
file held in AWS S3.</p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"d9201251-c45f-4b77-80d1-fc6f9f56e20d">The caller supplies=
 an <code>NHSD-Target-Identifier</code> header containing a base64-encoded =
<code>system</code> and <code>value</code>.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"f4551c99-28df-4c29-99e5-bc400d6e2ec7">The proxy decodes a=
nd validates the identifier.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"1b6b2f93-4341-4f45-9f6e-155d343979fc">The proxy retrieves=
 the routing file from private S3 using AWS Signature.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"5c813c3d-b6a2-4080-b490-c6dcf3afd938">The request path se=
lects an endpoint key, such as <code>appointment</code>, <code>slots</code>=
, <code>serviceRequest</code>, or <code>processMessage</code>.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"3c54336f-09bf-4495-9329-617a7c295686">BaRS uses the ident=
ifier and endpoint key to resolve the provider URL.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"73c66af4-b56d-4053-8c8a-8fa986d6e71e">The original path a=
nd query string are added to the URL, and the request is forwarded over mTL=
S.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"ba91fa3d-8bce-4019-b9c9-1fb4a888e0a3"><code>DocumentRefer=
ence</code> is an exception. It uses fixed NRLF consumer or producer routes=
 rather than the S3 routing file.</li>
</ul>
<p>The caller must already know which provider to target. BaRS resolves tha=
t provider; it does not search for every provider that may hold a patient's=
 data.</p>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"5.2." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-CurrentFlow.1">C=
urrent Flow</h2>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manu=
al-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" width=
=3D"468" src=3D"ef2a429e853047704fd325a6a66e1da7308354d88fc83b7372888ae1d4a=
c2f1e" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachments/1485019956/mermaid-flowchart=
-2026-08-27T19-49-49.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1787920388000&a=
mp;api=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D=
"1485019961" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=
=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"mermaid-flowchart-202=
6-08-27T19-49-49.png" data-base-url=3D"https://nhsd-confluence.digital.nhs.=
uk" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-co=
ntainer-id=3D"1485019956" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"1" tabi=
ndex=3D"0" alt=3D"" height=3D"1001"></span></p>
<p>Apigee first selects the route type. Static paths such as <code>/_ping</=
code> and <code>/metadata</code> are handled without a provider call, <code=
>DocumentReference</code> uses NRLF, and other supported resources use the =
S3-backed provider route.</p>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"5.3." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Considerations.3=
">Considerations</h2>
<p>Another team is planning to move or pull out the EPC flat file into its =
own service. This does not directly affect the WF integration or NHS Identi=
ty changes because it is downstream, but it may create uncertainty and plac=
e demands on the BaRS team for processes, documentation, and releases.</p>
<hr>
<h1 data-nh-numbering=3D"6." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-AppointmentsAPI&am=
p;Endpoints"><strong><u>Appointments API &amp; Endpoints</u></strong></h1>
<p>This section describes the Appointment API, booking flows, response beha=
viour, and the planned FHIR <code>_include</code> uplift.</p>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"6.1." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-CurrentImplement=
ation.4">Current Implementation</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"75b0dd78-f895-4f91-ad45-47f423664b6b">The production spec=
ification defines two Appointment read operations: <code>GET /Appointment</=
code> and <code>GET /Appointment/{id}</code>.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"d69e0907-83bf-4fde-8f88-26852a4f2482"><code>GET /Appointm=
ent</code> searches for appointments for a patient at a specific provider.<=
/li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"1e5fc53a-bee7-4696-a85c-ba9bd45c56cd"><code>GET /Appointm=
ent/{id}</code> returns one Appointment by its identifier.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"3ffb20a8-e5f9-42ac-824d-b595a65c3c9c">The caller supplies=
 the patient through the FHIR <code>patient:identifier</code> query paramet=
er and selects the provider with <code>NHSD-Target-Identifier</code>.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"5bdbb7f0-fb19-42cd-9424-940ba96d223d">The live proxy reso=
lves the provider endpoint from the S3 routing configuration and forwards t=
he request over mTLS.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"2f7a6414-fb29-4e52-a5ea-ace5d50621d7">The response from <=
code>GET /Appointment</code> is a FHIR <code>Bundle</code> with <code>type:=
 searchset</code>.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"ef198f8a-8068-4005-aac8-08055016913d">The response from <=
code>GET /Appointment/{id}</code> is a single FHIR <code>Appointment</code>=
 resource.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"72d18e7e-e313-481d-b782-f135d370624f">The specification d=
oes not define pagination, date filtering, status filtering, or a maximum r=
esult size.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"8ba669ec-caea-4d62-abce-a92f01d834ee">Booking, cancellati=
on, and appointment updates use <code>POST /$process-message</code> with a =
FHIR <code>MessageBundle</code>.</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"6.2." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-CurrentFlow.2">C=
urrent Flow</h2>
<p><strong>Endpoint Routing Diagram &amp; Route Table Can Be Found In The A=
ppendix</strong></p>
<h3 data-nh-numbering=3D"6.2.1." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Searchforappoi=
ntments">Search for appointments</h3>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manu=
al-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" width=
=3D"468" src=3D"4a92756828cde82f14528d42c7ca617c77f4e1410213148d6ae59363c82=
e4e19" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachments/1485019956/mermaid-flowchart=
-2026-08-27T09-41-04.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1787920388534&a=
mp;api=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D=
"1485019962" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=
=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"mermaid-flowchart-202=
6-08-27T09-41-04.png" data-base-url=3D"https://nhsd-confluence.digital.nhs.=
uk" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-co=
ntainer-id=3D"1485019956" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"1" tabi=
ndex=3D"0" alt=3D"" height=3D"301"></span></p>
<h3 data-nh-numbering=3D"6.2.2." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Readoneappoint=
ment">Read one appointment</h3>
<p><code>GET /Appointment/{id}</code> follows the same provider-resolution =
path, but returns a single Appointment resource.</p>
<h3 data-nh-numbering=3D"6.2.3." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Create,update,=
orcancelabooking">Create, update, or cancel a booking</h3>
<p><code class=3D"language-mermaid"><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file=
-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded=
-image" draggable=3D"false" width=3D"300" src=3D"8fe5a0651d6e950583fc90d927=
bd7e024cac1f28e6876a3cf059e5c17215fc0c" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachm=
ents/1485019956/mermaid-flowchart-2026-08-27T19-50-29.png?version=3D1&amp;m=
odificationDate=3D1787920389059&amp;api=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=
=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"1485019963" data-linked-resource-version=
=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-defaul=
t-alias=3D"mermaid-flowchart-2026-08-27T19-50-29.png" data-base-url=3D"http=
s://nhsd-confluence.digital.nhs.uk" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"im=
age/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"1485019956" data-linked-resou=
rce-container-version=3D"1" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" height=3D"936"></span><=
/code></p>
<p>The booking workflow uses <code>$process-message</code> for booking mana=
gement.</p>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"6.3." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-ResponseandError=
Behaviour">Response and Error Behaviour</h2>
<h3 data-nh-numbering=3D"6.3.1." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Responses">Res=
ponses</h3>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"confluenceTable">
  <thead class=3D"">
   <tr class=3D"">
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Operation</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Response</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Notes</th>
   </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody class=3D"">
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><code>GET /Appointment</code></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">FHIR <code>Bundle</code> with <code>type: se=
archset</code></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Contains matching Appointment resources.</td=
>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><code>GET /Appointment/{id}</code></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">FHIR <code>Appointment</code></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">The provider determines whether the Appointm=
ent exists.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><code>POST /$process-message</code></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Provider-defined FHIR response</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Used for booking and booking-management mess=
ages.</td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<h3 data-nh-numbering=3D"6.3.2." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Errors">Errors=
</h3>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"d023f9a2-f1e3-4480-88cb-cc4b0ad62316">Missing or invalid =
authentication is handled by Apigee before the provider call.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"6a56779b-4708-4803-941d-e7c1afc2eeac">Missing required re=
quest headers or invalid Target Identifier values produce proxy-level error=
s.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"8cd52f25-d3d4-410d-8392-ff693bd9fdc7">An unknown provider=
 or endpoint produces a proxy-level not-found response.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"70fbe14f-eb0b-48c5-b560-dbb290dfb5d4">Provider errors suc=
h as not found, unavailable, timeout, or mTLS failure are mapped or passed =
through according to the live proxy fault handling.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"399c4b48-49ac-4f61-8ed9-2890cce1e58c">The proxy normalise=
s many errors into FHIR <code>OperationOutcome</code> responses.</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"6.4." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-IntendedFutureBe=
haviour.1">Intended Future Behaviour</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"1f2b7d4d-f21e-4f25-a3bd-ed4ed4f0f11f">The planned FHIR <c=
ode>_include</code> uplift will allow an appointment search to return linke=
d or referenced resources in the same response Bundle.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"feec10e2-37cd-4daa-a486-f1e006efbc76"><code>_include</cod=
e> should follow standard FHIR search behaviour, with included resources re=
turned as additional Bundle entries rather than embedded directly inside th=
e Appointment resource.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"a4b17d7a-7341-4b4d-a8de-a9fd9ccc324d">Existing search beh=
aviour should remain unchanged when <code>_include</code> is not supplied.<=
/li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"e66e14f8-39d6-47df-8308-a20dcb3001a6">The uplift to inclu=
de _include may increase appointment retrieval volume and provider fan-out.=
</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"6.5." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-ChangesNeeded.2"=
>Changes Needed</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"43ca6481-9a29-4473-ba1e-4be9a82620d4"><strong>OpenAPI and=
 BaRS Standard:</strong> Document <code>_include</code>, supported referenc=
e paths, response semantics, invalid-value handling, and provider obligatio=
ns.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"cdf4199b-7478-4b47-b13b-5275ed0d13a7"><strong>Provider ca=
pabilities:</strong> Confirm that providers can return the requested refere=
nced resources and follow the same FHIR Bundle semantics.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"0f1761ee-1c54-403c-9a38-479e3b11502a"><strong>Response li=
mits:</strong> Reassess pagination, date/status filters, maximum Bundle siz=
e, and other controls because <code>_include</code> can increase response s=
ize.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"357ac83d-de78-435d-832e-ae75d28aec25"><strong>Errors:</st=
rong> Define the response when <code>_include</code> is unsupported, invali=
d, or refers to a resource that cannot be found.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"aa53a23f-370d-4039-8559-56b449285efc"><strong>Testing:</s=
trong> Add contract and integration tests for supported values, duplicate r=
eferences, missing references, invalid values, large responses, and request=
s without <code>_include</code>.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"81c7764c-003d-4e26-b983-8393ed3c9228"><strong>Performance=
:</strong> Measure response size, latency, provider load, rate-limit impact=
, and memory use with and without <code>_include</code>.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"6eda25d1-6ddf-4bcf-9605-a8f4214c91ff"><strong>Documentati=
on:</strong> Update examples, endpoint guidance, provider conformance guida=
nce, and supporting documentation.</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"6.6." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-CurrentRisks.3">=
Current Risks</h2>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"confluenceTable">
  <thead class=3D"">
   <tr class=3D"">
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Risk</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Potential impact</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Evidence or mitigation</th>
   </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody class=3D"">
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Appointment search results are unbounded</td=
>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Large responses may increase latency, transf=
er time, memory use, and client processing.</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">The specification has no pagination, date fi=
lter, status filter, or maximum result size.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Retrieval is provider-specific</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">A caller must know which provider to ask bef=
ore making the request.</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">There is no federated search. Multiple provi=
ders require multiple calls and client-side aggregation.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Provider behaviour is outside BaRS</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Providers may differ in filtering, response =
time, error detail, or FHIR support.</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Define provider conformance expectations and=
 test representative receivers.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><code>_include</code> may enlarge already-un=
bounded responses</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Linked resources may multiply response size =
and provider work.</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Define supported includes and response-size =
controls before enabling the uplift.</td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"6.7." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Future-StateRequ=
irements.1">Future-State Requirements</h2>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"confluenceTable">
  <thead class=3D"">
   <tr class=3D"">
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Requirement</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">What must be resolved</th>
   </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody class=3D"">
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><code>_include</code> contract</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Define supported values, reference paths, re=
peat behaviour, and response structure.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Linked-resource access</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Ensure included resources are within the aut=
horisation scope of the original appointment search.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Response-size control</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Decide whether pagination, filters, maximum =
Bundle size, or another limit is needed.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Performance target</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Set targets for latency, response size, prov=
ider load, concurrency, and error rate after the addition of _include</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Backwards compatibility</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Confirm that requests without <code>_include=
</code> and existing consumers continue to behave as before.</td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"6.8." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Considerations.4=
">Considerations</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"c95c0c92-cd63-4a6a-9bb8-20e40d84bf2e"><code>patient:ident=
ifier</code> identifies the patient being searched for; <code>NHSD-Target-I=
dentifier</code> identifies the provider to query.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"1a364324-38d6-45b1-9fa6-7d547289c913">An Appointment path=
 identifier is an Appointment ID, not a patient NHS number.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"4eed1477-1e82-41c3-90bb-14748bccc3fa">The current API ret=
urns all matching appointments for the selected provider, so <code>_include=
</code> may increase the size of an already potentially large result.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"a67eb6c2-3fcc-40f3-aab2-3b77d393b5e9">The current route u=
ses S3 to resolve provider endpoints. The planned EPC service change may af=
fect endpoint capability information later, but it is outside this API upli=
ft.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"9d115378-3604-41ff-b2da-c99630aa68bd">Existing authentica=
tion is application-level. PF patient authorisation is covered in the Authe=
ntication and Security sections and should not be duplicated here.</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"6.9." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-OpenQuestions.2"=
>Open Questions</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"38244e1c-6000-436e-88d2-9cd216f02096">Which <code>_includ=
e</code> values are required for the first release?</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"a719ac66-b734-4eb3-836c-7b3f630f660c">Should the uplift s=
upport only direct references, or also recursive or chained includes?</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"f2681154-54e6-4c57-84d1-109232a3ff15">How should duplicat=
e references and missing referenced resources be represented in the Bundle?=
</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"78454924-21bf-4709-9b3e-e6d06f16fcf7">What should happen =
when a provider does not support <code>_include</code> or receives an inval=
id value?</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"b430c661-abf1-4a77-b062-1078d43511ee">Should <code>_inclu=
de</code> be available on all endpoints or only specific ones?</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"0fe51cd4-8fbf-4934-b863-03b93dd5fd4a">Are pagination, dat=
e filtering, status filtering, or a maximum Bundle size required before <co=
de>_include</code> is enabled?</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"475438f0-2f32-4245-b541-af709140335a">What happens when a=
 provider does not support _include, receives an invalid value, or cannot f=
ind a referenced resource?</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"b035ee81-7cc5-4471-8abb-36d9817482a6">What contract and i=
ntegration tests are needed for supported values, duplicates, missing refer=
ences, and requests without _include?</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h1 data-nh-numbering=3D"7." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Questions"><strong=
><u>Questions</u></strong></h1>
<p>This section brings together the unresolved questions raised across the =
review, grouped by subject area.</p>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"7.1." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-PFAuthentication=
andAuthorisation">PF Authentication and Authorisation</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"83fac67b-560f-4375-8bff-0347dcd96fe0">Does the exchanged =
token preserve the delegation information BaRS needs?</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"57731dc8-88c9-4941-b4e5-65845444fa6e">Which claims identi=
fy the subject, actor, and delegation?</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"aff56429-7feb-48c0-9406-f57339d0bfc1">Which endpoints req=
uire patient matching, and how should the NHS number be extracted from sear=
ches and <code>$process-message</code> Bundles?</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"b64e72cc-6b19-4392-80b9-9ff74fe7ffa0">Where should the pa=
tient-authorisation decision be made?</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"c06034c6-c41e-4df4-ad26-c5fcb2527df0">What response shoul=
d BaRS return when delegation is missing, invalid, expired, or does not mat=
ch the requested patient?</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"0866d322-b344-41e2-8941-e648d18cc8bd">Should any end-user=
 context or token be passed to providers?</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"7.2." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-AppointmentAPIan=
d_include">Appointment API and&nbsp;<code>_include</code></h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"62acda5d-000c-41e0-ae23-7a12e7293165">Which <code>_includ=
e</code> values and reference paths are required for the first release?</li=
>
 <li data-uuid=3D"21f7ed9b-e377-4357-9ee9-8cb6571f3d56">Should <code>_inclu=
de</code> support only direct references, or also recursive or chained incl=
udes?</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"1985091f-f380-4e15-a85a-72280541befa">Should <code>_inclu=
de</code> be available on <code>GET /Appointment</code> only, or on other s=
earch endpoints as well?</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"379e3a8d-17d9-4ff7-aab1-eec7d51a251a">How should duplicat=
e references and missing referenced resources appear in the FHIR Bundle?</l=
i>
 <li data-uuid=3D"af7928b6-cb70-468d-b01b-419dc6eab015">What should happen =
when a provider does not support <code>_include</code> or receives an inval=
id value?</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"f7565867-66d3-4a06-86d6-6d411083dc7e">Are pagination, dat=
e filtering, status filtering, or a maximum Bundle size required before <co=
de>_include</code> is enabled?</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"44d3c165-a940-4faa-b8d7-81589d3df42c">What changes are re=
quired to the BaRS Standard, OpenAPI specification, examples, and provider =
conformance processes?</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"7.3." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-EPCandEndpointDi=
scovery">EPC and Endpoint Discovery</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"78653706-f368-4fd1-97bc-d36e09d66a34">When will the futur=
e EPC service replace the current S3 routing file?</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"f3074d96-8f1f-4927-a19e-94fade6a53d3">Which team will own=
 the EPC service, its availability, and its provider data?</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"7.4." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-ScalabilityandRe=
silience">Scalability and Resilience</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"b987b11b-1100-4b31-a736-6efb80c9771e">Are the existing ra=
te limits and timeouts still appropriate after <code>_include</code> is int=
roduced?</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"7.5." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Security,Operati=
ons,andOwnership">Security, Operations, and Ownership</h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"54281466-be7e-40a3-8215-a2b6b8889c4c">Who owns the proces=
s of documentation, releases &amp; specification updates?</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"7a5ee81a-751a-4f02-b5ea-6fac9aca76cf">What operational pr=
ocesses, documentation, incident flows, and recovery procedures are require=
d after PF auth conversion?</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h1 data-nh-numbering=3D"8." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-Risks"><strong><u>=
Risks</u></strong></h1>
<p>This section brings together the current and future risks identified acr=
oss the review, grouped by theme.</p>
<h2 data-nh-numbering=3D"8.1." id=3D"BaRSTechnicalDeepDive-SecurityandDataP=
rotection">Security and Data Protection</h2>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"relative-table confluenceTable" style=3D"width: 53.6795%;"=
>
  <colgroup class=3D"">
   <col class=3D"" style=3D"width: 18.6848%;">
   <col class=3D"" style=3D"width: 29.6811%;">
   <col class=3D"" style=3D"width: 51.4835%;">
  </colgroup>
  <thead class=3D"">
   <tr class=3D"">
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Risk</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Potential impact</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Current position / mitigation</th>
   </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody class=3D"">
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Sensitive values may be logged</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">OAuth tokens, client assertions, NHS numbers=
, target identifiers, or FHIR data could be exposed in logs or traces.</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">The Splunk shared flow is external. <code>JC=
-AWSSignV4.xml</code> also has <code>debug=3Dtrue</code>. Confirm logging b=
ehaviour, redaction, retention, and access controls.</td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
